    "summary": "The configurator won't put a drawer and a spike at the same corner of one cell, so that part of the brief can't be built as asked. A drawer goes on the cut face of a half base, so I placed a north half base at (1,0,0) and added a drawer there. I tried a spike at the corner on the drawer side where cells (0,0), (1,0) and (0,1) meet. It was refused with SPIKE_CLASH: \"a drawer (south half) fills this corner of the junction, where the spike would stand.\" Instead I put the spike at another corner of the same cell, where cells (0,0), (1,0) and (1,-1) meet. That puts both parts on cell (1,0,0), but not at the same corner. I removed the extra cell (0,1), capped the open faces and bolted the joints. check_build shows no issues and the collision check is clear.",
